{"stamp": "1790716427500039508-743627", "tool": "file_read", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"file_path": "target/Mathlib/Data/Finset/Defs.lean", "line_start": 30, "line_end": 62}, "result_chars": 1536}
{"stamp": "1790716440468873017-744134", "tool": "lean_verify_edit", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"path": "Mathlib/Data/Finset/Defs.lean", "line_start": 34, "line_end": 55, "replacement": "More information can be found in `Mathlib/Algebra/BigOperators/Group/Finset/Defs.lean`.\n\nFinsets are directly used to define fintypes in Lean.\nA `Fintype α` instance for a type `α` consists of a universal `Finset α` containing every term of\n`α`, called `univ`. See `Mathlib/Data/Fintype/Defs.lean`.\n\n`Finset.card`, the size of a finset is defined in `Mathlib/Data/Finset/Card.lean`.\nThis is then used to define `Fintype.card`, the size of a type.\n\n## File structure\n\nThis file defines the `Finset` type and the membership and subset relations between finsets.\nMost constructions involving `Finset`s have been split off to their own files.\n\n## Main definitions\n\n* `Finset`: Defines a type for the finite subsets of `α`.\n  Constructing a `Finset` requires two pieces of data: `val`, a `Multiset α` of elements,\n  and `nodup`, a proof that `val` has no duplicates.\n* `Finset.instMembership`: Defines membership `a ∈ (s : Finset α)`.\n* `Finset.instSetLike`: Provides a coercion `s : Finset α` to `s : Set α`, and through\n  `SetLike` a coercion of `s : Finset α` to the type of all `x ∈ s`."}, "result": {"mode": "verified_edit", "success": true, "errors_introduced": 0, "errors_already": 0, "environment_reviewed": false}}
{"stamp": "1790716452006841623-745023", "tool": "precedent_search", "exit": 0, "arguments": {"code": "In the future, we could consider generalizing `Finset.Nat.antidiagonalTuple` further to\nsupport finitely-supported functions, as in `Finset.finsuppAntidiag` from\n`Mathlib/Algebra/Order/Antidiag/Finsupp.lean`.", "limit": 5}, "result_chars": 5736}
